.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA UPGRADE COMPATIBLE-VERSIONS" "1" "2026-08-18" "0.39.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa upgrade compatible-versions Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-upgrade\-compatible-versions \- List software versions compatible with a...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa upgrade compatible-versions
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List software versions compatible with a group of ASA devices.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to query.
.TP
\fB\-\-per\-device\fP
Include per-device version breakdown in output.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
